{
  "name": "Papierkram — a voucher from an email attachment",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "postProcessAction": "nothing",
        "downloadAttachments": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "3f7a1b10-0003-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Email (IMAP)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailReadImap",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "voucher",
        "operation": "create",
        "name": "={{ $json.subject }}",
        "provenance": "domestic",
        "lineItems": "={{ JSON.stringify([{ name: $json.subject, amount: 0, vat_rate: '19%', category: 'Bürobedarf' }]) }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "documentDate": "={{ $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "3f7a1b10-0003-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Create voucher",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-papierkram.papierkram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "voucherDocument",
        "operation": "create",
        "voucherId": "={{ $json.id }}",
        "binaryPropertyName": "attachment_0"
      },
      "id": "3f7a1b10-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Upload attachment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-papierkram.papierkram",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A voucher from an email attachment\n\nThe IMAP trigger needs **Download Attachments** switched on; the file then arrives in `attachment_0`. With Gmail the field is named differently depending on the node settings — whatever it is goes into *Input Binary Field*.\n\nThe order matters: the voucher first, the attachment second. The ID from the first step goes into *Voucher ID* in the second.\n\n`category` and `vat_rate` are account-specific **names**, not codes or percentages, and are spelled as Papierkram spells them. To see the valid ones, run *Voucher → Get Many* once and look at `line_items`.\n\nThe amount is 0 here: the real value comes either from an OCR step before this, or from finishing the voucher in Papierkram.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "3f7a1b10-0003-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        160
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Email (IMAP)": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Create voucher",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Create voucher": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Upload attachment",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "pinData": {}
}
